The 'PUT_AddContract' method is expected to add a new element to the ArrayList. It should produce valid output contracts whenever possible input contracts are satisfied. This test method should include the following checks:
    
   - The input contracts are valid for the current method under test.
   - The result of the method under test is an increase in the count by one.
   - The index of the item after adding is the same as the last index of the item.

In this case, you want to test the ArrayList contract verification after adding a new element. In order to achieve this, you need to include the following assertions:
    
